	<key>Age, moulting, daylight, stress and nutrition can change egg numbers. Compare daily records over several weeks rather than assuming disease from one low day. Straining, weakness or a swollen abdomen need prompt veterinary assessment. Do not attempt to remove an egg yourself.</key>
