	<key>Check feather bases, skin and coop crevices for irritation or tiny moving specks. Pale combs, feather damage and reduced laying can have many causes. Record what you see and ask a poultry veterinarian to identify the problem before treatment. Keep bedding clean and inspect the rest of the flock.</key>
